trajectory.patch:
The Kconfig warning indicates a dependency issue. The test-specific Kconfig file for the power domain test is missing a dependency for its configuration option. Additionally, there is a logical error in the device tree overlay where a test device is assigned to the wrong power domain, which would cause a test failure at runtime.

Here are the fixes for both issues:

tests/subsys/pm/power_domain/Kconfig
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
# Copyright 2025 NXP
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

source "Kconfig.zephyr"

config TEST_PM_DEVICE_ISR_SAFE
	bool "Use ISR safe PM for the test"
========
# Copyright (c) 2023 NXP
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

source "Kconfig.zephyr"

config TEST_PM_DEVICE_ISR_SAFE
	bool "Use ISR safe PM for the test"
	depends on PM_DEVICE
>>>>>>>> REPLACE
tests/subsys/pm/power_domain/app.overlay
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
	test_dev_b: test_dev_b {
		compatible = "test-device-pm";
		status = "okay";
		power-domains = <&test_domain_balanced>;
	};
========
	test_dev_b: test_dev_b {
		compatible = "test-device-pm";
		status = "okay";
		power-domains = <&test_domain>;
	};
>>>>>>>> REPLACE
